1
00:00:00,110 --> 00:00:03,351
Napoleon brought more than half a million men.

2
00:00:04,127 --> 00:00:07,774
The Russian armies refused him the battle he needed.

3
00:00:08,550 --> 00:00:13,621
They retreated instead, and burned the supplies behind them as they went.

4
00:00:14,397 --> 00:00:19,332
It was the largest invasion force assembled in Europe up to that point.

5
00:00:20,108 --> 00:00:25,246
He reached Moscow in September and found something no conqueror plans for.

6
00:00:26,022 --> 00:00:27,433
The city was empty.

7
00:00:28,209 --> 00:00:30,908
Almost the entire population had left.

8
00:00:31,684 --> 00:00:34,721
There was nobody there to surrender to him.

9
00:00:35,497 --> 00:00:38,603
A conqueror needs somebody to accept defeat.

10
00:00:39,378 --> 00:00:42,077
There was nobody left in the building.

11
00:00:42,853 --> 00:00:46,704
That night, fires started in several districts at once.

12
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:52,822
The city's firefighting equipment had been removed before the French arrived.

13
00:00:53,597 --> 00:00:56,771
Most of the city was still built out of wood.

14
00:00:57,546 --> 00:01:01,465
Over four days, roughly three quarters of Moscow burned.

15
00:01:02,241 --> 00:01:08,057
Whether an order was given, or the fires spread from looting, is argued to this day.

16
00:01:08,833 --> 00:01:10,922
The effect was not ambiguous.

17
00:01:11,697 --> 00:01:16,904
The governor of the city had ordered the fire pumps removed before he left.

18
00:01:17,679 --> 00:01:21,395
Napoleon held the capital and gained nothing from it.

19
00:01:22,170 --> 00:01:26,631
No supplies, no winter shelter, no government to negotiate with.

20
00:01:27,407 --> 00:01:31,461
He waited five weeks for a peace offer that never arrived.

21
00:01:32,237 --> 00:01:34,326
The retreat began in October.

22
00:01:35,102 --> 00:01:39,969
Of the men who marched into Russia, only a small fraction marched out.

23
00:01:40,745 --> 00:01:47,578
The army that had beaten every power in Europe was destroyed by a city that refused to be occupied.

24
00:01:48,353 --> 00:01:53,085
Cold, hunger and constant attack finished what the fire had started.

25
00:01:53,861 --> 00:01:57,576
A century later the empire collapsed from the inside.

26
00:01:58,352 --> 00:02:04,168
Nineteen seventeen brought revolution, and with it a decision that reversed Peter's.

27
00:02:04,944 --> 00:02:09,744
The Bolsheviks moved the capital back to Moscow in nineteen eighteen.

28
00:02:10,519 --> 00:02:14,303
The imperial eagles came down from the Kremlin towers.

29
00:02:15,078 --> 00:02:18,523
Red Square became the stage of a global ideology.

30
00:02:19,298 --> 00:02:25,589
Moscow was now the centre of a state that intended to remake the entire world in its image.

31
00:02:26,365 --> 00:02:31,774
Foreign delegations came to study it, and foreign governments came to fear it.

32
00:02:32,550 --> 00:02:39,179
In the nineteen thirties the eagles were replaced with red stars of ruby glass, lit from inside.

33
00:02:39,955 --> 00:02:43,941
They are still up there, and they still turn in the wind.

34
00:02:44,717 --> 00:02:52,431
And then, for the fourth time in its history, an army came for this city with the stated intention of ending it.

35
00:02:53,206 --> 00:02:59,158
In the autumn of nineteen forty one, German forces advanced to within sight of Moscow.

36
00:02:59,934 --> 00:03:04,259
Some units reached the last tram stop on the edge of the city.

37
00:03:05,035 --> 00:03:10,106
Officers could see the buildings of the city through their field glasses.

38
00:03:10,881 --> 00:03:13,174
The city did not fully evacuate.

39
00:03:13,949 --> 00:03:15,632
Factories kept running.

40
00:03:16,408 --> 00:03:23,579
Civilians dug anti tank ditches by hand, and in December, in extreme cold, the Red Army counterattacked.

41
00:03:24,355 --> 00:03:32,475
The military parade on Red Square went ahead that November, and the troops marched from it directly to the front line.

42
00:03:33,251 --> 00:03:35,950
The advance stopped there permanently.

43
00:03:36,725 --> 00:03:45,320
It was the first major failure of that army, and it happened at the gates of a city that had already survived three burnings.

44
00:03:46,096 --> 00:03:49,743
What followed was construction on an enormous scale.

45
00:03:50,519 --> 00:03:56,742
Wide avenues, a metro built like a palace, and seven towers that still define the skyline.

46
00:03:57,517 --> 00:04:03,334
Much of it was raised by a population that had just lost tens of millions of people.

47
00:04:04,109 --> 00:04:14,195
And in December nineteen ninety one the flag above the Kremlin came down, and the state that had built all of it ceased to exist, almost overnight.

48
00:04:14,970 --> 00:04:16,788
Moscow absorbed that too.

49
00:04:17,564 --> 00:04:28,192
Today it holds more than twelve million people, and the towers of its financial district stand a few kilometres from walls raised in the fourteen hundreds.

50
00:04:28,967 --> 00:04:33,970
The two sit inside the same skyline, and neither one looks out of place.

51
00:04:34,746 --> 00:04:39,410
Look at the whole sequence at once and the pattern is hard to miss.

52
00:04:40,186 --> 00:04:41,801
Burned by the Mongols.

53
00:04:42,576 --> 00:04:44,123
Burned by the Tatars.

54
00:04:44,899 --> 00:04:46,514
Occupied by the Poles.

55
00:04:47,289 --> 00:04:49,582
Burned again in eighteen twelve.

56
00:04:50,358 --> 00:04:52,582
Besieged in nineteen forty one.

57
00:04:53,358 --> 00:04:55,989
Five times destroyed or nearly taken.

58
00:04:56,765 --> 00:05:05,020
Five times rebuilt, on the same hill, above the same river, by people who kept deciding the position was worth the risk.

59
00:05:05,796 --> 00:05:08,631
That is not really a story about empire.

60
00:05:09,406 --> 00:05:17,594
It is a story about a decision made over and over, usually by ordinary people standing in ash, choosing to start again.

61
00:05:18,370 --> 00:05:20,391
Moscow was never inevitable.

62
00:05:21,167 --> 00:05:22,307
It was rebuilt.

63
00:05:23,083 --> 00:05:31,000
Thank you for watching, and if you want the next chapter of this history, tell us in the comments where to go next.

